title: Payers › Process › Add and edit conditions
route: /payers/summit?tab=process
intro: A condition sends a case down another path when it is true. Each condition has four parts: what is tested, the value, the kind of step it leads to, and what happens. The sentence shown on the workflow card is built from the first two.
dir: TD
---
start s1 "In the 'Edit workflow' drawer,\nclick 'Add a condition' under a step"
process nw "New condition row appears\nProgram is Residential 3.5 leads to a File step\n'What happens' blank"
screen row "Condition row\nCondition on, value, Leads to,\n'What happens on this path', bin"

group gP "Pick what is tested"
  input a1 "Pick 'Condition on'\nProgram, Request type, Portal status,\nTime waiting, Payer answer"
  process a2 "Value resets to the first value of that kind\nso the pair always makes sense"
  input a3 "Pick 'Condition value'"
  process a4 "Program: Residential 3.5, IOP, PHP, Detox, IOP or PHP\nRequest type: an initial request, a continued-stay request,\na retro-authorization, a recertification, an appeal\nPortal status: down, slow, asking for a new sign-in\nTime waiting: 24 hours, 2 business days, 3 business days\nPayer answer: approves, denies or partly approves, asks for information"
endgroup

input b1 "Pick 'Leads to'\nChecklist, File, Portal or Phone step"
input b2 "Type 'What happens'\nExample: Caller phones and logs who it spoke to"
process nochk "No check for blank text\nThe condition would show with an empty line"
click rm "Click the bin\n'Remove this condition'"
process rm2 "Condition row disappears at once"

process rd "How it reads on the workflow card after Save\nProgram: 'If program is Residential 3.5'\nRequest type: 'If request is a retro-authorization'\nPortal status: 'If portal is down'\nTime waiting: 'If no status after 2 business days'\nPayer answer: 'If payer approves'"

process cnt "Footer count goes up by one\nfor each added, changed or removed condition"
goto g1 "Continues in: Payers › Process › Save the workflow"

s1 --> nw --> row --> a1 --> a2 --> a3
a3 -.-> a4
a3 --> b1 --> b2 --> cnt
b2 -.-> nochk
row --> rm --> rm2 --> cnt
cnt --> g1
a3 -.-> rd
